course: dictionary
lesson: 3045
title: Earwax: a helpful, yucky word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Earwax is the soft yellow or brown waxy stuff that your body makes inside the ear canal, the tube that leads to your eardrum. It may sound yucky, but it is a helpful part of you. «Earwax traps dust, helps keep germs out and moves out by itself as you chew and talk.»
explain: Earwax protects your ears in two ways: it catches dust and germs, and it keeps the skin inside your ear from drying out. So when a text says earwax protects the ear, it means earwax keeps the ear safe from harm.
explain: Doctors say you should not push cotton buds inside your ears. «Cotton buds often push it deeper.» Pushing can also hurt the eardrum. Your ears usually clean themselves, so leave them alone and ask a grown-up if you think there is a problem.
fact: Earwax is a natural part of the body, and it is made inside the ear canal.
fact: «Earwax protects and cleans your ears by itself.»
fact: Cotton buds, also called cotton swabs or Q-tips, can push earwax deeper and hurt the eardrum, so doctors say not to put them inside your ears.
fact: Earwax can be dry and flaky or wet and sticky, and one gene decides which type a person has.
fact: A «build-up of earwax» means too much wax has collected in the ear. «Ear drops» are drops put into the ear, often to soften the wax.
exercise: «Earwax traps dust, helps keep germs out.» What job does earwax do here? | *Catches dust and germs | Tastes sweet | Makes your ears sing | Makes you hear louder
exercise: What is earwax? | A type of cotton bud | *A soft, waxy substance the body makes inside the ear canal | Bone inside the ear | A germ that makes ears itch
exercise: Why should you not push cotton buds inside your ears? | Ears need cotton buds to stop dust | Cotton buds make wax taste bad | *They can push wax deeper and hurt the eardrum
test: «Earwax protects your ear by keeping the skin from drying out.» What does protects mean? | Makes it wet | Cleans your teeth | *Keeps safe from harm | Hides it from view
test: What does «build-up of earwax» mean? | A packet of cotton buds | A small drop of medicine | *Too much wax collected in the ear
exam: Ravi says earwax is dirt that you must dig out every day with a cotton bud. Which answer is best? | Dig it out daily, the more the better | Earwax is a kind of germ | *Earwax cleans and protects the ear and usually moves out by itself | Cotton buds clean the ear best
